From 765903ea26e473826b2fcf32dbe984b30649f47b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:24:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci: name native-memory-macos as a push-triggered
 sub-workflow in ci.yaml header

After #1455, native-memory-macos.yml is a workflow_call lane that keeps
its own push: main trigger, like hermes-state-macos. The header comment
named only hermes-state-macos as the exception.

Comment-only change (review nit, COMMENT review 5877935078 on #1455).
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yaml | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yaml b/.github/workflows/ci.yaml
index 5b2d3d5533..09d1f49173 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yaml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yaml
@@ -7,8 +7,9 @@ name: CI
 #
 # Sub-workflows are triggered via ``workflow_call`` and keep their own job
 # definitions, matrices, and concurrency settings. They no longer have
-# ``push:`` / ``pull_request:`` triggers of their own, except hermes-state-macos:
-# it keeps standalone main validation, masked out of this workflow on main pushes.
+# ``push:`` / ``pull_request:`` triggers of their own, except hermes-state-macos
+# and native-memory-macos: each keeps standalone main validation (its own
+# ``push:`` trigger), masked out of this workflow on main pushes.
 #
 # SECURITY: this workflow runs PR-controlled actions, workflows, and code.
 # Do not add ``secrets: inherit`` or GitHub App credentials here. Trusted
-- 
2.43.0

